-- g1-application.l4: s.5 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or Air-Conditioning Systems Law
-- 5785-2025 (Sefer HaChukim 3349 p. 183), the application for a licence or its renewal.  Group G1.
-- Imports prelude, daydate and domain.  The Hebrew is copied by script from inputs/law.wiki (src:N is line N);
-- identifiers and glosses are mine and the Hebrew governs.
--
-- s.5 states no period: not for the application, not for the Registrar's demand, not for the publication.  So no
-- rule here carries a WITHIN (a period the Law does not enact would be invented).  A regulation under s.60(2)(a)
-- may fix the time for an application to renew; none is in the sources (IP14), and no rule here needs it.
-- The fee (Fees Regulations, reg.4) bars the Registrar from GRANTING or RENEWING a licence unless it was paid;
-- it does not bar the submission of an application, so IP11 is consumed where a licence is granted (G2) and not here.

§ `Chapter 2: Licensing (continued)`

§§ `s.5 Application for a licence or for its renewal`

-- The acts of s.5: the applicant's, and the Registrar's two.
@desc The acts of section 5: the applicant submits an application; the Registrar may require information or a document and must publish how to apply
DECLARE `Act under section 5` IS ONE OF
    `submit a licence application to the Registrar`
    `require information or a document from the applicant`
    `publish on the Ministry website how to apply for a licence and the documents to attach`

-- s.5(a), the first words: "Whoever seeks to obtain or to renew a licence under this Law (in this Law: applicant)".
-- The definition of "applicant" is a test on the person: they seek to obtain a licence, or to renew one.
-- src:79 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} המבקש לקבל או לחדש רישיון לפי הוראות חוק זה (בחוק זה – מבקש), יגיש בקשה לכך לרשם (בחוק זה – בקשה לרישיון).
@ref s.5(a) (src:79)
@desc The facts about a person that decide whether they are an applicant under s.5(a)
DECLARE `Facts about a person and a licence under section 5` HAS
    `seeks to obtain a licence under the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person seeks to obtain a licence under the Law
    `seeks to renew a licence under the Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person seeks to renew a licence under the Law

@ref s.5(a) (src:79)
@export True if the person is an applicant under section 5(a): they seek to obtain a licence under the Law or to renew one
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a person and a licence under section 5` @desc What the person seeks
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(a) — the person is an applicant` person MEANS
        person's `seeks to obtain a licence under the Law`
    OR  person's `seeks to renew a licence under the Law`

-- The definition of "licence application" (in the Law: בקשה לרישיון): the application the applicant submits to the Registrar.
@ref s.5(a) (src:79)
@desc The facts about a request that decide whether it is a licence application under s.5(a)
DECLARE `Facts about a request under section 5` HAS
    `submitted to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the request was submitted to the Registrar
    `submitted by an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the request was submitted by an applicant under s.5(a)

@ref s.5(a) (src:79)
GIVEN request IS A `Facts about a request under section 5`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(a) — the request is a licence application` request MEANS
        request's `submitted to the Registrar`
    AND request's `submitted by an applicant`

-- s.5(a): "shall submit".  A duty in form, with no period and no consequence the Law names: it is the step without
-- which no licence is granted.  Kept as a MUST with no WITHIN; the reading that s.5(a) only DEFINES "applicant"
-- and "licence application" and adds no duty is the other reading (a fork), and is what the two predicates above say.
@ref s.5(a) (src:79)
GIVEN person IS A `Facts about a person and a licence under section 5`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under section 5`
`s 5(a) — the applicant must submit a licence application` person MEANS
    IF   `s 5(a) — the person is an applicant` person
    THEN PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST `submit a licence application to the Registrar`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant`
               BECAUSE "section 5(a): the applicant did not submit an application to the Registrar"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s.5(b): the Registrar may require of the applicant any information or document he needs to decide the application.
-- "Needed by him" is the Registrar's own judgement: an input.
-- src:80 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} הרשם רשאי לדרוש מהמבקש כל מידע או מסמך הדרושים לו לשם קבלת החלטה בבקשה לרישיון.
@ref s.5(b) (src:80)
@desc The facts section 5(b) asks before the Registrar may require information or a document
DECLARE `Circumstances of a demand under section 5(b)` HAS
    `the demand is made of an applicant on a licence application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the demand is made of an applicant, on a licence application before the Registrar
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or document is needed to decide the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's opinion: True if the Registrar needs the information or document in order to decide the application

@ref s.5(b) (src:80)
@export True if section 5(b) lets the Registrar require the information or document of the applicant: the demand is made of an applicant on a licence application and, in the Registrar's opinion, the information or document is needed to decide it
GIVEN demand IS A `Circumstances of a demand under section 5(b)` @desc The facts of the demand and the Registrar's opinion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Registrar may require the information or document` demand MEANS
        demand's `the demand is made of an applicant on a licence application`
    AND demand's `in the Registrar's opinion the information or document is needed to decide the application`

@ref s.5(b) (src:80)
GIVEN demand IS A `Circumstances of a demand under section 5(b)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under section 5`
`s 5(b) — the Registrar may require information or a document` demand MEANS
    IF   `the Registrar may require the information or document` demand
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `require information or a document from the applicant`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s.5(c): the Registrar shall publish on the Ministry website the ways to submit the application and the list of
-- documents to attach to it.  No period is stated.
-- src:81 | {{ח:תת|(ג)}} הרשם יפרסם באתר האינטרנט של המשרד את הדרכים להגשת הבקשה לרישיון ורשימת מסמכים שיש לצרף לה.
@ref s.5(c) (src:81)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under section 5`
`s 5(c) — the Registrar must publish how to apply and the documents to attach` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    MUST `publish on the Ministry website how to apply for a licence and the documents to attach`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Registrar`
          BECAUSE "section 5(c): the Registrar did not publish on the Ministry website how to apply for a licence and the list of documents to attach"
